kind: vulnerability
title: "FortiClient EMS API authentication bypass CVE-2026-35616 exploited to push the EKZ infostealer to managed endpoints"
headline: "Attackers used FortiClient EMS flaw CVE-2026-35616 to plant a VPN on-connect script that runs an infostealer on every managed endpoint"
summary: "Fortinet disclosed CVE-2026-35616 on 2026-04-04, an API authentication and authorization bypass in FortiClient EMS 7.4.5 and 7.4.6 (CVSS 9.8), marked it known exploited, and fixed it in 7.4.7 and hotfixes; CISA listed it on 2026-04-06. Arctic Wolf reported on 2026-05-27 that attackers used it to edit an EMS remote-access profile so that every managed FortiClient ran a script on VPN connect, which delivered the EKZ infostealer disguised as a Fortinet patch."
event_date: 2026-05-27
priority: notable
immediate_action: null
